# Copy to .env.local. Values: Supabase, Project Settings → API.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...
# No database URL: the app reaches the database only through the Supabase HTTPS API (.claude/rules/db.md).
# The secret key (Project Settings → API Keys → secret) bypasses RLS: server jobs without a user session only
# (createAdminClient in *.admin.ts), never NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
# Second factor (TOTP) for everyone. In production (Vercel Preview too) it is required unless the value is exactly false;
# locally it is off unless true. Commented out on purpose: importing this file into Vercel must not turn it off.
# AUTH_REQUIRE_MFA=true
# Scheduled jobs (/api/cron/*): at least 32 random characters (openssl rand -base64 32), checked by isCronRequest
# (src/shared/lib/cron.ts). Empty means /api/cron/* refuses. Set it in Vercel with the first scheduled job.
CRON_SECRET=
# Server errors; empty turns Sentry off (local, CI). EU region (docs/release.md).
SENTRY_DSN=
# Vercel production and preview set it themselves; staging needs SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=staging.
# SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=
# Source map upload on Vercel builds; without them stack traces point to minified code.
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
# SENTRY_ORG=
# SENTRY_PROJECT=
# Test user for screens behind sign-in (Playwright MCP): .env.test.local, which Claude may read unlike .env.local,
# or environment variables; then npm run seed:test-user and npm run totp -s (.claude/rules/tests.md).
# TEST_USER_EMAIL=
# TEST_USER_PASSWORD=
# base32, at least 26 characters (16 bytes), e.g. JBSWY3DPEHPK3PXPJBSWY3DPEHPK3PXP; empty means no second factor.
# TEST_USER_TOTP_SECRET=
